{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>I am the Elohim of your father.</b> He revealed to him that his father had died, therefore it writes 'the Elohim of your father.' For HaShem does not attach His name to the righteous during their lifetimes, but only at their death, because 'He does not trust His holy ones' — therefore He revealed to him now his father's death, so that he would not refuse to accept greatness; for before Aaron his brother he would refuse to accept greatness, before his father all the more so." "<b>And Moshe hid his face.</b> As reward for <b>ויסתר</b> (and he hid), he merited a radiant countenance. As reward for <b>כי ירא</b> (for he was afraid), he merited that they fear to approach. As reward for <b>מהביט</b> (from looking), he merited 'the form of HaShem he beholds.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:58.370914475Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}